                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "managerId is captured but not being used?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/manager_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 109,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for finding this.\nFor the current single bmc support logic, it will be treated as NotFound if managerId != DEFAULT_BMC.\nModified `afterGetValidManagerPath()` to check it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 657,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "In the original if no bmc is found an error is not being returned. But here it will be treating it as an error. Was that not the reason for the revert?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 657,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "You're right.\nPreviously, `getManagerObject()` checks the NotFound condition and bypasses this `getManagerData()` - https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/d9495964cd857f8775677f3f5c1f35f0cf00c0a6/redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp#L889C5-L889C21\n\nSo, it would be correct here not to treat as an error."
                }
            ],
